---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Unity House Centres — UK Programme" description="Unity House Centres is a proposed UK public-benefit programme. Visio Nova Mundi is preparing a community-focused initiative in East London.">
  <section class="heroBlock">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Proposed UK programme · Community engagement growing</p>
      <h1>Unity House Centres</h1>
      <p class="lead">A proposed UK community resource and support model being developed by Visio Nova Mundi CIC. We are starting with careful listening, local relationships and practical community engagement.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Discuss a proposed partnership</a><a class="btn" href="#community-engagement">Get involved locally</a></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="statusCard"><p class="statusLabel">Current status</p><h2>Designed for local adaptation</h2><p>Unity House is being shaped as a repeatable model. Any future activity will depend on appropriate partners, safeguards, evidence and readiness.</p><span class="statusPill">No centres currently operating</span></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section communityUpdate" id="community-engagement">
    <p class="eyebrow">Stage 1 · East London community engagement</p>
    <h2>Listening and building local relationships</h2>
    <p>Visio Nova Mundi is preparing a new community-focused initiative in East London, with an initial focus on connecting with Romanian-speaking residents while remaining open to people from other local communities.</p>
    <p>We want to learn directly from residents about healthy living, access to affordable food, community connection, language barriers and the kinds of local support people would find genuinely useful.</p>
    <p>We are also looking for <strong>Romanian-speaking and Romanian-English volunteers and community connectors</strong> who would like to help us reach residents, support communication and gather community feedback.</p>
    <div class="volunteerRow">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Interested in helping?</p>
        <p class="volunteerBoundary">Volunteers may support Romanian-English communication, community introductions, welcoming residents, approved outreach, simple feedback collection and identifying practical needs and barriers. This is a community-support role, not a clinical or professional nutrition role.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Contact Visio Nova Mundi</a>
    </div>
    <p class="safeguard"><strong>This community-engagement activity does not represent an operating Unity House Centre or an approved food-surplus programme. Unity House remains in development.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
      <p class="eyebrow">What we are learning</p>
      <h2>Community insight before larger claims</h2>
      <p>Alongside our community conversations, Visio Nova Mundi intends to learn more about practical barriers to healthy food, community engagement, language accessibility and what residents would value from future community-food services.</p>
      <p class="note"><strong>These community insights will inform future Unity House feasibility work, but will not be presented as proof that a future service is ready to operate.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Stage 2 · Future Unity House Centres model</p>
      <h2>Local proof first, potential UK replication later</h2>
      <p>Unity House Centres is intended to be locally adaptable rather than dependent on one locality or building. Each proposed node would begin with a real local need and an appropriate host, then be shaped around the resources, safeguards and partners available in that place. A permanent centre would only be considered after a hosted model has produced credible evidence.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow"><div><strong>1</strong><span>One evidenced local need</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>One trusted host</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>One suitable resource stream</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>Appropriate partners</span></div><div><strong>5</strong><span>Responsible coordination</span></div><div><strong>6</strong><span>Evidence and learning</span></div></div>
    <p class="formula">1 evidenced local need + 1 trusted host + 1 suitable resource stream + appropriate partners + responsible evidence = 1 testable local Unity House node</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid section">
    <article class="card highlight"><p class="eyebrow">Future concept</p><h2>Food-Surplus Core remains proposed</h2><p>Food is one possible future resource stream within the wider Unity House concept. Any future development would require evidence, suitable partners, safety controls and readiness gates before activity could begin.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Why start small?</p><h2>Learn before considering replication</h2><p>The immediate priority is listening to residents and understanding local needs. No operating service, impact figures or outcomes are being claimed in advance.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section class="section boundary">
    <div class="sectionHead"><p class="eyebrow">Responsible development</p><h2>What the current programme does not claim</h2><p>Before any Unity House activity could begin, host responsibilities, safety, insurance, safeguarding, data protection, logistics, evidence and governance would all need to be confirmed through readiness gates.</p><p class="note"><strong>Unity House does not aim to replace community organisations that already work. It is being designed to connect, support and learn from existing local capability.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="cards four"><article class="smallCard"><h3>No operating centres</h3><p>Unity House Centres is a proposed programme. No physical centre is currently operating.</p></article><article class="smallCard"><h3>No fixed resource stream</h3><p>Future resource streams would be considered only where evidence and partners support them.</p></article><article class="smallCard"><h3>No automated eligibility</h3><p>People would not be selected or rejected by AI, and sensitive data would be minimised.</p></article><article class="smallCard"><h3>No invented proof</h3><p>Planning assumptions and future ambitions remain separate from real community evidence.</p></article></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section supportBar"><div><h2>Would you like to get involved?</h2><p>We are looking for careful conversations with residents, volunteers, community connectors and potential hosts who can help us understand local needs responsibly.</p></div><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Contact Visio Nova Mundi</a></section>
  <p class="controlNote"><strong>Current status:</strong> A separate East London community-engagement activity is being prepared. Unity House Centres and any future food-surplus concept remain proposed and are not yet operational.</p>

  <style>
    .heroBlock{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.25fr .75fr;gap:18px;align-items:start}.eyebrow{margin:0 0 9px;color:#0f766e;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}h1{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,64px);letter-spacing:-.04em;color:var(--text)}.lead{margin:0;max-width:72ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:19px}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-radius:14px;padding:11px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:white;color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font-weight:850}.btn.primary{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.10),rgba(16,185,129,.10));border-color:rgba(39,99,235,.25)}.btn:hover{border-color:rgba(0,0,0,.18);text-decoration:none}.statusCard,.card,.smallCard,.supportBar{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:18px;background:white;box-shadow:0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.05)}.statusCard{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.07),rgba(16,185,129,.07))}.statusLabel{margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}.statusCard h2,.card h2,.supportBar h2{margin:0 0 9px;color:var(--text);font-size:21px;letter-spacing:-.02em}.statusCard p,.card p,.smallCard p,.supportBar p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.statusPill{display:inline-block;margin-top:14px;padding:7px 10px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.25);color:#0f766e;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}.section{margin-top:34px}.sectionHead h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:29px;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--text)}.sectionHead>p:not(.eyebrow){margin:0;max-width:90ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.sectionHead>.note{margin-top:12px!important;font-size:13px}.communityUpdate{padding:22px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.24);border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(16,185,129,.08),rgba(39,99,235,.06))}.communityUpdate h2{margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--text);font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.025em}.communityUpdate>p:not(.eyebrow):not(.safeguard){color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.volunteerRow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;margin-top:18px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.2)}.volunteerBoundary{margin:0;max-width:72ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.safeguard{margin:18px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border-left:3px solid #d97706;background:rgba(245,158,11,.09);color:var(--text)!important;line-height:1.7}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;align-items:start}.highlight{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.06))}.note{margin-top:12px!important;font-size:13px}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:16px}.flow div{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:13px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(39,99,235,.04);color:var(--text);font-weight:750}.flow strong{display:grid;place-items:center;flex:0 0 28px;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(39,99,235,.12);color:#1d4ed8}.formula{margin:14px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.18);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(16,185,129,.06);color:var(--text);line-height:1.6;font-weight:750}.boundary{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:25px}.cards.four{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:14px}.smallCard{padding:14px}.smallCard h3{margin:0 0 7px;color:var(--text);font-size:16px}.smallCard p{font-size:14px}.supportBar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.06))}.supportBar>div{max-width:75ch}.controlNote{margin:18px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border-left:3px solid #d97706;background:rgba(245,158,11,.09);color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;font-size:13px}@media(max-width:1100px){.flow{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:900px){.heroBlock,.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.flow,.cards.four{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.supportBar,.volunteerRow{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch}}@media(max-width:520px){.flow,.cards.four{grid-template-columns:1fr}.communityUpdate{padding:18px}.supportBar{padding:16px}.btn{width:100%}}
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
